Conversely the Yukawa threshold \(q_*^2=q_b^2\) at \(\hat U>0\) requires an uncancelled tadpole of size \(|T|=F\hat U\chi^4/(32\pi^2m^8)\) in the same convention. Second, taken alone and not cancelled, \(U_4\) contributes \(\mathcal M=F\sqrt{|g|}\hat U\chi^4/256\pi^2\), of the sign that pulls \(q_*^2\) positive for \(\hat U>0\), and \(q_*^2=6\sqrt{|g|}\hat U\chi^2m^6/(\hat V+2\hat T)\); its ratio to \(q_b^2\) is \(\sqrt{|g|}m^8/2\), and the comparison of magnitudes turns on the conventions for \(m\) and \(\sqrt{|g|}\) and is not settled here.
